5.5 Viability kernel (Aubin)

Controlled dynamical system

\dot x(t) = f(x(t), u(t), w(t)), \qquad x(t) \in \mathcal{X},\; u(t) \in \mathcal{U},\; w(t) \in \mathcal{W}.

Constraint set

K = K_{F1} \cap K_{F2} \cap K_{F3} \cap K_{F4} \cap K_{F5}.

Viability kernel

\mathrm{Viab}_K = \left\{\, x_0 \in K \;:\; \exists u(\cdot)\ \text{s.t.}\ x(t; x_0, u, w) \in K \ \forall t \in [0,T],\ \forall w \in \mathcal{W} \,\right\}.

Non-emptiness of $\mathrm{Viab}_K$ — not of the static intersection K — is the correct statement of lunar viability. This document does not claim $\mathrm{Viab}_K \neq \varnothing$; §10 specifies the pipeline by which the question is investigated.

