10.2 Tier-1 specification

State vector:

x = \big(P_{\text{cabin}}, E_{\text{storage}}, X_{\text{H}_2\text{O}}, X_{\text{O}_2}, K_{\text{critical}}, G\big).

Initial conditions:

x_0 = (101.3\ \text{kPa},\ 1.00,\ 90\ \text{d},\ 60\ \text{d},\ 0.95,\ 1).

Horizon: $T = 180$ days. Resupply window $[90, 180]$ with launch-failure hazard $\lambda = 0.10\ \text{yr}^{-1}$.

Disturbances:

· Equipment failure: exponential inter-arrival, $\mu_{\text{fail}} = 0.05\ \text{day}^{-1}$.
· Dust event: Poisson, $\lambda_{\text{dust}} = 0.02\ \text{day}^{-1}$, reducing $E_{\text{storage}}$ by 5–15%.
· Crew illness: two-state Markov, $\mu_{\text{ill}} = 0.02\ \text{day}^{-1}$, $\mu_{\text{rec}} = 0.10\ \text{day}^{-1}$, reducing effective maintenance capacity 40%.

Nominal control policy $u_{\text{nominal}}$:

· Maintain $P_{\text{cabin}} \geq 70$ kPa by N₂/O₂ make-up.
· Maintain $X_{\text{H}_2\text{O}} / X_{\text{O}_2}$ above 1.5× safety floor.
· Request resupply when $X_{\text{H}_2\text{O}} < 30$ d remaining.
· Trigger F5 mitigation (pre-delegated authority) when no binding decision in 48 h.

10.3 Reference algorithm

```python
# lus_tier1.py — reference implementation (algorithmic specification)
# Tier-1 Monte Carlo for Lunar University System viability kernel study.
# Output: Ŷ = P(failure before T) with bootstrap CI, per failure mode.

def simulate_one_run(rng, dt=0.05, T=180.0):
    x = init_state()                    # §10.2
    t = 0.0
    while t < T:
        w = sample_disturbances(rng, dt)  # equipment, dust, illness
        u = u_nominal(x, t)               # §10.2 policy
        x = f(x, u, w, dt)                # controlled dynamics
        if violated(x):                   # F1–F5 thresholds
            return failure_mode(x), t
        t += dt
    return None, T

def monte_carlo(N=10000, seed=20260925):
    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)
    failures = [simulate_one_run(rng) for _ in range(N)]
    Y_hat = sum(1 for m, _ in failures if m is not None) / N
    # Per-mode breakdown
    per_mode = {F: sum(1 for m, _ in failures if m == F)/N for F in [F1,F2,F3,F4,F5]}
    # Bootstrap CI
    ci = bootstrap_ci(failures, statistic="mean", n_boot=2000)
    return Y_hat, per_mode, ci
```

