14. CENTRAL THESIS

\boxed{\;\text{The first extraterrestrial civilizations will require new functions because their infrastructure combines physical, biological, computational, and institutional systems with no exact terrestrial equivalent.}\;}

The primary innovation is the educational architecture required to produce people capable of operating coupled civilization-scale systems:

\text{University} \to \text{Systems Laboratory} \to \text{Civilization Simulator} \to \text{Institutional Memory}.

A university that teaches 20 new functions before it can keep 144 peas alive for 14 days will not be funded.

\boxed{\;\text{Prove the peas, then prove the pressure vessel, then prove the governance.}\;}

